From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:04:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: also clear RG_SEM_SKIPPED without an RG semaphore
 interrupt

The CPU-side clear of the display RG_SEM_SKIPPED error event only ran
from the RG semaphore interrupt handler, i.e. only while an RG semaphore
interrupt was pending. Disabling the vblank RG semaphore now really stops
its interrupt, so a skip latched just before DRM turned vblank interrupts
off stayed set until the next vblank enable, with the GSP spinning on it
and the GPU clocks at max meanwhile.

Move the check to kdispServiceLowLatencyIntrs_KERNEL(), so it runs on
every display interrupt CPU-RM services (including RM vblank callbacks,
e.g. NVKMS vblank semaphore control), and also run it from a 1 Hz RM
callback registered at display state load, which covers the time when no
display interrupt arrives at all. The 1 Hz callbacks run with the GPU
lock held and are skipped while the GPU isn't at full power. Reads of
0xffffffff or a 0xbadXXXXX PRI error are ignored. The log line now says
which path cleared the event.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
